# Template for the cloudflared tunnel-token Secret. Copy to secret.env (gitignored),
# paste the real token, then seal it (secret.env never leaves your machine; only the
# encrypted sealed-secret.yaml is committed):
#   ./scripts/seal-secret.sh cloudflared
# secret.env is matched by .gitignore so it can never be committed.
#
# IMPORTANT: bare KEY=value — NO surrounding quotes, no trailing spaces.
# kubectl --from-env-file stores the value literally (quotes included), which would
# corrupt the token. The token is one long opaque string with no spaces, so paste it
# raw right after the = sign.
#
# Where the token comes from (Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard):
#   Networks -> Tunnels -> <your tunnel> -> Configure -> it's the long value after
#   `--token` in the install command. Treat it like a password: it authorizes the
#   tunnel. If you rotate it in the dashboard, re-run the seal script and push.
TUNNEL_TOKEN=